<!--
    kuna infrastructure test: S7 region-identification observability
    (KunaRegionIdentifier, ported from angr's RegionIdentifier; see
    docs/regions.md).

      region tree    - nested region tree (angr GraphRegion.dbg_print analog)
      region blocks  - flat regions_by_block_addrs lists
      region walk    - recursive region-order walk over every leaf block
      phase map      - routes the surfaces to P7 / loop-refinement

    Reuses the gh8724-arraystride bytes purely as a loadable loop+diamond CFG
    (the arraystride option itself is never touched):

      B0 0x3c0  entry `test rsi,rsi; je 0x418`  -> {B1, B4}
      B1 0x3c5  setup                           -> B2
      B2 0x3e0  single-block loop body, `jne 0x3e0` self-loop -> {B2, B3}
      B3 0x40a  epilogue/ret
      B4 0x418  early-out ret

    The identifier must find the self-loop as a cyclic region at 0x3e0 (this
    exercises angr's infinite-self-loop slice hack, RI l.109), root the tree
    at the entry 0x3c0, and walk each block exactly once.

    SEAM(W7) Inc 0: the tree is now built from the REAL bblocks CFG via
    KunaRegionIdentifier::build_from_block_graph (block start addresses, the CFG
    out-edges, and the per-block endsWithBranchindOrCbranch lastOp probe), not
    the old synthetic-node stub.  Assertions #6-#8 pin the resulting tree:
    the top region keeps THREE distinct nodes: the CBRANCH-ending entry 0x3c0
    (never folded into the diamond because its last op is a CBRANCH), the nested
    region rooted at 0x3c5, and the early-out 0x418 - exactly the supergraph
    shape only the branchind/cbranch-aware real adapter produces; the nested
    region at 0x3e0 pairs the cyclic self-loop with its 0x40a exit/epilogue.

    Analysis-only: the region commands never mutate the function; default
    decompiler output is unchanged (hence no docs/divergences.md entry).
-->
